messages:
Eleni: Quick QA note — noticed the icon-only buttons in the compact table toolbar have poor contrast in dark theme and the touch hit area is under 44px. Screenshot: https://imgur.com/redwood/compact-icon-contrast.png

Marcus: repro? Browser/os? I can run it locally.

Eleni: macOS Safari, compact density. The svgs are using token color.icon-muted which ends up at ~2.4:1 on dark background. Also padding is 4px so overall clickable area is about 36x36.

Priya: token callout: spacing.icon-button is currently 4px for compact; we should add spacing.icon-button-compact=10px so min hit area becomes 44. That will ripple to lists and the table toolbar. I'll draft a token PR.

Diego: also we need to handle contrast without making icons visually too heavy. Proposal: switch icon-only color to color.icon-strong (token) in dark theme and keep color.icon-muted for light theme. Add a subtle filled hover state for affordance.

Eleni: accessibility name: these icon buttons are tooltip-only today. Make sure every icon-only button has aria-label (e.g. aria-label="Filter rows") and tooltip text matches. For row-scoped actions include context: aria-label="Pin row: {{rowTitle}}" so screen readers know which row.

Marcus: good. Tests: axe will flag contrast and missing name. I'll add storybook stories for light/dark compact toolbar with axe snapshots. Also add an e2e that taps icon area on mobile sizes.

Priya: token PR will include migration notes and a CSS vars map. We'll add spacing.icon-button-compact: 10px and var(--spacing-icon-button-compact). Also check tooltip offsets because larger hit targets will affect layout.

Diego: CSS snippet for proposed changes:
```css
.icon-btn {
  padding: 10px; /* token: spacing.icon-button-compact */
  min-width: 44px;
  min-height: 44px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  color: var(--color-icon-muted); /* light theme */
}
[data-theme=dark] .icon-btn {
  color: var(--color-icon-strong); /* token to increase contrast */
}
.icon-btn:focus-visible {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--color-focus);
  outline: none;
}
.icon-btn[aria-label]::after { /* tooltip handled by JS */
  /* no-op: ensure tooltip text equals aria-label */
}
```

Eleni: also recommend adding a small filled ripple on hover for icon-only in dense contexts so users get a stronger affordance when they hover/tap. Use background fade instead of strong color change.

Marcus: I'll add unit tests: aria-label presence, contrast ratio >= 3:1 for icons on both themes, and a visual regression for the hover/focus states. e2e: simulate keyboard focus and touch events at narrow viewport.

A11yBot: auto-checker: when PR is opened run contrast-suite and name-presence checks. Tag @Priya @Diego on failures.

Priya: I'll include device screenshots (iOS + Android) with before/after spacing and token mapping.

Diego: plan: I'll implement CSS + tooltip binding (ensure tooltip text comes from aria-label), Marcus adds tests, Priya lands token PR. Eleni will validate the UX and sign off.

Eleni: thanks all :raised_hands: — this should address the low-contrast and hit-target issues without changing visual hierarchy too much.
